.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_CAP_DELAYED 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_cap_time ,
.Nm dtfl_cap_delayed ,
.Nm dtfl_cap_try_delayed ,
.Nm dtfl_cap_downgrade ,
.Nm dtfl_cap_try_downgrade ,
.Nm dtfl_cap_clone ,
.Nm dtfl_cap_drop ,
.Nm dtfl_cap_output
.Nd capabilities to send timely dataflow output
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft "const uint64_t *"
.Fn dtfl_cap_time "const dtfl_cap *c"
.Ft dtfl_cap *
.Fn dtfl_cap_delayed "const dtfl_cap *c" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft dtfl_cap *
.Fn dtfl_cap_try_delayed "const dtfl_cap *c" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_cap_downgrade "dtfl_cap *c" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_cap_try_downgrade "dtfl_cap *c" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft dtfl_cap *
.Fn dtfl_cap_clone "const dtfl_cap *c"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_cap_drop "dtfl_cap *c"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_cap_output "const dtfl_cap *c"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A capability lets an operator send output at a timestamp and keeps
timely's progress tracking from advancing past that time until the
capability is released.
Each capability holds one unit of its time in its output's internal
count for its whole life; clone adds another, drop removes one, and
downgrade moves it to a later time.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_cap_time
returns the capability's time, a vector of the scope's class.
.Fn dtfl_cap_output
returns the output port it is for.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_cap_delayed
returns a new capability at
.Fa t ,
which must be greater than or equal to the capability's time.
.Fn dtfl_cap_try_delayed
is the same but returns
.Dv NULL
rather than panicking when
.Fa t
is not beyond the current time.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_cap_downgrade
advances the capability in place to
.Fa t ,
which must be greater than or equal to its current time.
.Fn dtfl_cap_try_downgrade
is the same but returns
.Dv DTFL_EINVAL
rather than panicking.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_cap_clone
returns an independent capability at the same time, which must also be
dropped.
.Fn dtfl_cap_drop
releases a capability.
Failing to drop a capability stalls progress tracking.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_cap_time
returns the capability's time words, and
.Fn dtfl_cap_output
its output port.
.Fn dtfl_cap_delayed ,
.Fn dtfl_cap_try_delayed
and
.Fn dtfl_cap_clone
return a new owned capability;
.Fn dtfl_cap_try_delayed
returns
.Dv NULL
when
.Fa t
is not beyond the current time.
.Fn dtfl_cap_try_downgrade
returns 0 on success or
.Dv DTFL_EINVAL .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_cap *cap = dtfl_op_initial_cap(op, 0);
uint64_t next = dtfl_cap_time(cap)[0] + 1;
dtfl_cap *later = dtfl_cap_delayed(cap, &next);
/* ... send output at `cap` and `later` ... */
dtfl_cap_drop(later);
dtfl_cap_drop(cap);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_EINVAL
.It Bq Er DTFL_EINVAL
.Fn dtfl_cap_try_downgrade
was given a time that is not greater than or equal to the capability's
current time.
.El
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_cap_delayed
and
.Fn dtfl_cap_downgrade
treat the same condition as a contract violation and call the panic hook
.Pq Xr dtfl_set_panic_hook 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_op_builder_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_op_input_next 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_time_cmp 3
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C form of timely's
.Vt Capability
and
.Vt InputCapability
.Pq capability.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A capability belongs to the worker thread that minted it and must not be
shared across threads.
